# 🔐 Social Login (Google, Twitter, Facebook) with JWT in Node.js

Here's a **complete, step-by-step guide** to integrate social login (OAuth) into your mental health web app using **Passport.js + JWT** in Node.js.

---

## 🧠 How It Works (The Flow)

The authentication mechanism uses **OAuth 2.0**, supported by most social identity providers including Facebook, Google, Twitter, etc. Once the server returns the profile details of the user, you store them in your database and return **JWT tokens** to the client. The JWT tokens are then used for authentication, irrespective of what medium (email or social auth) the user used for initial login.

**Visual Flow:**
```
User clicks "Login with Google"
        ↓
App redirects to Google/Facebook/Twitter
        ↓
User grants permission
        ↓
Provider sends back profile data to your callback URL
        ↓
Your server creates/finds user in DB
        ↓
Your server issues a JWT → sent back to client
        ↓
Client uses JWT for all future API requests
```

---

## 📦 Step 1: Install Dependencies

